      "date": "2026-05-23T20:25:58.000Z",
      "title": "New major risk - Revenue and earnings growth",
      "body": "Earnings have declined by 2.0% per year over the past 5 years. This is considered a major risk. Ultimately, shareholders want to see a good return on their investment and that generally comes from sharing in the company's profits. If profits are declining over an extended period, then in most cases the share price will decline over time unless the company can turn around its fortunes. A trend of falling earnings can be very difficult to turn around. If the company is well already established it may also be a sign the company has matured and is in decline. In addition, if the company pays dividends it will also likely need to reduce or cut them, striking a dual blow to total shareholder returns. Currently, the following risks have been identified for the company: Major Risk Earnings have de",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "0e708285-32f3-4bc3-839d-5f7cb8ae1a6c",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-05-23T20:25:57.000Z",
      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings released: EPS: ₹18.09 (vs ₹10.95 in FY 2025)",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹18.09 (up from ₹10.95 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹5.99b (up 11% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹186.8m (up 65% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 3.1% (up from 2.1% in FY 2025). The increase in margin was driven by higher revenue. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has fallen by 27% per year but the company’s share price has increased by 2% per year, which means it is well ahead of earnings.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
